====Adjective====
{{en-adj|-}}

# Of a period of time, being particular.
#: {{ux|en|'''One''' day the prince set forth to kill the dragon that had brought terror to his father’s kingdom for centuries.}}
#* {{RQ:Churchill Celebrity|chapter=4|passage='''One''' morning I had been driven to the precarious refuge afforded by the steps of the inn, after rejecting offers from the Celebrity to join him in a variety of amusements. But even here I was not free from interruption, for he was seated on a horse-block below me, playing with a fox terrier.}}
# Being a [[single]], [[unspecified]] thing; [[a]]; [[any]].
#: {{ux|en|My aunt used to say, "'''One''' day is just like the other."}}
# [[sole|Sole]], [[only]].
#: {{ux|en|He is the '''one''' man who can help you.}}
#: {{ux|en|The '''one''' male audience member at the concert is invited on stage.}}
# [[whole|Whole]], [[entire]].
#: {{ux|en|Body and soul are not separate; they are '''one'''.}}
# In agreement.
#: {{ux|en|We are '''one''' on the importance of learning.}}
# The same.
#: {{ux|en|The two types look very different, but are '''one''' species.}}

