{{en-part}} {{lb|en|Singlish|Manglish}}

# {{non-gloss|[[use#Verb|Used]] at the [[end#Noun|end]] of a [[sentence#Noun|sentence]] to [[highlight#Verb|highlight]] the [[characteristic#Noun|characteristics]] of someone or something.}}
#: {{uxi|en|[[got#Etymology 2|Got]] almonds '''one'''.|There are almonds in it.}}
#: {{uxi|en|How come so heavy '''one''' [[ah#Etymology 2|ah]]?|Why is it so heavy?}}
#: {{uxi|en|Can '''one''', why cannot?|Of course you can.}}
#: {{uxi|en|Need to take train '''one'''.|You can only get there by taking the train.}}
#: {{uxi|en|Can easily get lost '''one''', [[know#Etymology 3|know]]?|You can easily get lost here/there.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=w:Patricia Mok|newspaper=w:The Straits Times|series=Life! section|location=Singapore|publisher=w:Singapore Press Holdings|date=14 February 2000|page=5|oclc=47722736|text='My boyfriends very possessive '''one'''. They don't allow me to wear clothes I want, do things I want,' she laments.}}
#* {{quote-newsgroup|en|author=Ethical Egoist|newsgroup=soc.culture.singapore|year=2004|passage=Why so special '''one'''?}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2014|author=Cheryl Lu-Lien Tan|title=Singapore Noir|publisher=Akashic Books|isbn=9781617752353|page=89|passage=These fish, {{l|en|ah|id=separator}}, anything also eat '''one'''. Small fish, each other, anything you throw in also they take.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=w:Jean Tay|title=Sisters & Senang: The Island Plays|year=2018|isbn=9789814785907|section=Scene 9|page=62|publisher=Epigram Books|passage=Only sweet hands can draw sweet water, you know that. If I take the water myself, sure salty '''one'''.}}
#* {{quote-web|en|author=Justin Vanderstraaten|work=ricemedia.co|date=14 January 2020|quotee=Moon|title=Drugs, Cash, and Prison. When Does Enough Become Enough?|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20240226222606/https://www.ricemedia.co/culture-people-drugs-cash-prison-enough-become-enough/|archivedate=26 February 2024|text=When I was a kid, [[kena#Etymology 2|kena]] [[rotan]] also cannot learn '''one''' but when I had peace of mind, it was easy.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Syarafana Shafeeq|quotee=w:Royston Tan|newspaper=w:The Straits Times|title=NDP 2023: Film-maker Royston Tan wants to correct ‘small regret’ in 2nd outing as creative director|location=Singapore|publisher=w:Singapore Press Holdings|date=27 June 2023|oclc=47722736|text=For me, I’m very drama '''one''' {{l|en|lah|id=attitude}}. I just want it to be very big, and to display our theatrics.|archivedate=24 July 2023|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20230724000508/https://www.straitstimes.com/singapore/filmmaker-royston-tan-intends-to-correct-small-regret-in-second-outing-as-ndp-creative-director}}
# {{senseid|en|originator}}{{non-gloss|Used at the end of a sentence to highlight the [[originator]] of something.}}
#: {{uxi|en|My friend send '''one'''.|It was sent by my friend.}}
#: {{uxi|en|Who say '''one'''?|Who said so?}}
#: {{uxi|en|He ask '''one''', not I ask '''one'''.|It wasn’t me who asked, it was him.}}
#* {{quote-newsgroup|en|author=Singrish King|newsgroup=soc.culture.singapore|year=2011|passage=ooooooooooar! you own self admit '''one''' [[ah#Particle|har]]! i never say '''one''' har!}}
# {{non-gloss|A [[nominalizer]] used to form a [[noun phrase]] without a [[w:head (linguistics)|head noun]].}}
#: {{uxi|en|The sell fruits '''one''' go home [[already]].|The fruit seller went home.}}

